      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So, like a \"solo\" feature in sound editing software?\nI dig this idea, it would be helpful for Never Have I Ever and other games that require a host.\nBut I have to agree with Wolfine, a bad implementation would encourage users to close themselves off and only listen to friends even more, that's bad in a social game.\nIn case of Never Have I Ever, a better approach would be to automate this process. Maybe by defining a host through votes or through a trigger placed in the map?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-02T10:11:14.174Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "like mute but in reverse, a way to prevent a selected user from hearing oneself, with two modes, \"all but (user)\" and \"list\" when you want to speak privately but you/they don't want to/can't leave a world. this would make communicating privately to a select few in crowded places easier or when you only want to talk to one person.\nand to wrap up, leaving a world turns itself off/empties the list for convenience in case of forgetting.",
